      "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
      "notes": "ArcGIS Server layer MapIndy/MapIndyProperty/MapServer/10 'Parcel' (ArcGIS Online item 0d28e222479743baa97f8f4456da7bb4 'Parcels w/ Owner Information & Assessed Values', updated nightly from IndyGIS Parcels and the Assessor): 347,057 polygons; maxRecordCount 1000. The files are 21 pages (OBJECTID order, geometry off) of the polygons whose Indiana DLGF property class (PROPERTY_SUB_CLASS) is 300-499 (industrial 3xx and commercial 4xx; 20,866 polygons). One tax parcel (STATEPARCELNUMBER) can cover several polygons with the same values. FULLOWNERNAME joins up to four name lines with ', '. No roll year in the layer (ASSESSORYEAR_* are the current assessment year's land, improvement and total assessed value). gis.indy.gov serves no robots.txt (404). The data.indy.gov / indianamap.org hubs have Crawl-delay 60 and are not used. The statewide IndianaMap parcel layer (gisdata.in.gov Parcel_Boundaries_of_Indiana_Current, 3,682,675 parcels) carries DLGF property class and situs but no owner and no values, so the county layer is better for Marion."
